-- 2026-10-06: the thinking behind the Yak Sports and Ice & Gold proposals, written after Cole asked
-- "did you analyze retention, last year, early BF vs lockdown vs just an offer?" Sources: Fireflies
-- (Yak Aug 21, Sep 3, Oct 2; Fela Oct 1), Locus (Ice & Gold 60-day TW read, weekly report), Slack.
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO p_season_answer (act_id, season, key, value) VALUES
 ('act_2964926606966267','2026','strategy_note',
'WHAT WE KNOW (Yak Sports)
Wholesale brand first: about $1.8M wholesale projected, 27,000 hats to Dick''s, Golf Galaxy and Lids for 2027. The Shopify store did 429 orders year to date, mostly organic and wholesale spill. No paid DTC history, no returning-customer base to speak of, no real email list yet (J.C. runs email, Nick''s model comes later). Ads start Oct 15 to 19, so the pixel is 5 to 6 weeks old on Black Friday. Hoodie $78, about 73% gross margin, breakeven 1.43, target 2.5 (Rob, Oct 2). 13 colorways; black M and L low. Rob will not undermine pricing (retail partners).
WHAT WE DO NOT KNOW: last November and December in Shopify, list size, whether a bundle price under $78 a hoodie breaks a retail price agreement. Rob or McKenna answer all three in five minutes.

WHAT THAT MEANS
No lockdown, no members-only day: there is nobody to lock the store for. No early Black Friday sale either: a percent off in November teaches a brand-new audience that the price moves. This is a cold-acquisition launch that happens to run into Black Friday, so the job is one clean offer that protects price and makes the second hoodie easy: gift with purchase in November, a pair bundle on the weekend, gift set in December, and the 2027 hats as the reason to join the list.

THE PROPOSAL
Nov 6 to 25: buy any hoodie, pick a free snapback ($50 value). No markdown.
Nov 27 to 30: two hoodies for $140 + a free snapback (about 10% off the pair). If Rob says the pair price breaks retail parity: one hoodie + snapback + free shipping instead.
Dec 7 to 16: hoodie + hat gift set, gift wrapped, order-by date in every ad.
Dec 29 to Jan 5: list-only first look at the 2027 hats before retail gets them.
KPI: new customers and list size, not ROAS, until the pixel has 45 days.'),
 ('act_952386692927446','2026','strategy_note',
'WHAT WE KNOW (Ice & Gold)
Launched Oct 1 2023, so this is the third Black Friday but the first with us. Fela: nearly 60% of customers come back; influencer videos convert and the last agency''s creative did not. Last 60 days in Triple Whale: about $33.8k on $10.4k spend (3.3x), 260 orders, AOV about $130, 54% of revenue from new customers; September was the best month at $20.9k; last week $5.6k on $1.25k (4.45x). 18k gold plated jewelry $39 to $159; sets over-index on the Nigerian audience; 500 creators waiting, 60 videos in; a $16 gift-wrap product exists.
WHAT WE DO NOT KNOW: November and December 2024 and 2025 in Shopify (revenue, what offer ran, how deep), list size and email revenue share, product margins (onboarding form). Fela or Ayo answer the first two from Shopify in ten minutes; margins come from the form.

WHAT THAT MEANS
60% returning is exactly the profile where a members-first day pays, so Thursday early access for the list and past customers is right. Not a closed store, because the reason Fela hired us is NEW customers and Black Friday is the cheapest new-customer week of the year; the public site stays open. No early Black Friday sale: November builds the list with a gift (studs over $100), so the people who would have bought at 30% off in November buy at full price with a gift instead, and the whole list is warm for Thursday. The weekend offer is spend tiers, not a flat percent, because the $130 basket is the lever: $100/$200/$300 thresholds pull a one-ring order to two. December is gifting: sets, free wrap, gift cards. Valentine''s is the second season for jewelry and reuses the same mechanics.

THE PROPOSAL
Nov 2 to 25: join the list for early access Thursday + free pair of studs with a first order over $100. Creators film the gift reveal.
Thu Nov 26: list and past customers get the weekend offer 24 hours early (private link, site open).
Nov 27 to 30: spend $100 save $25, $200 save $60, $300 save $100, free gift box on every order. Alternative if Fela prefers: buy 2 pieces, get the 3rd free. One or the other, never both.
Dec 4 to 16: three gift sets (her, him, the pair) at full price, $20 off by email to BFCM buyers only; free gift wrap until the cutoff.
Dec 17 to 24: gift cards lead. Jan 14 to Feb 7: Valentine''s, same mechanics, list first.
KPI: new customers on the weekend, list growth in November, AOV on the tiers.');
